  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next` applies to it. The Workflow section's last step, step 7, names the next skills. After `habeas author --all` it says to follow the `habeas-evidence` skill, including its \"Disagreeing assessments\" section if assessments disagree. It then says to make any behavior or text changes under the `habeas-requirements` skill. Both skills are bundled: `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` and `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` have those names. The Gotchas section after the workflow is not part of the workflow, so it doesn't change where the workflow ends. The skill meets the obligation to end by naming the skill for the next task, and the outcomes that lead to different tasks are covered. The requirement lists no violation matches for this site.",
